    1: (P)ROM and BIOS emulation in GXemul:
    2: ------------------------------------
    3: 
    4: The general philosophy that applies to PROM/BIOS emulation is that no raw 
    5: binary dumps of real ROMs should be included in GXemul. It is nicer to 
    6: emulate in software only those parts of a machine's ROM or BIOS that are
    7: actually necessary to boot an operating system.
    8: 
    9: This directory contains software emulation of various PROMs and BIOSes.
   10: 
   11: (Note: Running actual PROM dumps may also be possible in a few cases.
   12: Using the -Q command line option disables GXemul's software emulation
   13: of the PROM and allows raw PROM dumps to be used.)

