12649: 
12650:                                              Internal Register Summary C-3
12651: Table C-3 is a summary of the I/O controller registers.
12652: 
12653:                                           Programming Note
12654: 
12655:      The IOC register address (34-bit) range is 180000000 through
12656:      1BFFFFFFF, and the IOC registers are sparsely populated in this
12657:      range. Although the IOC internally decodes only a subset of the
12658:      34-bit address to access the IOC registers, Digital recommends that
12659:      programs use only the addresses specified in Table C-3 to ensure
12660:      correct operation in future implementations.
12661: 
12662: Table C-3 I/O Controller Registers
12663: 
12664: Mnemonic     Register Name              Address      Reset State and
12665:                                         1 8000 0000  Required Initialization
12666: IOC_HAE      Host address extension     1 8000 0020
12667: IOC_CONF     Configuration cycle type   1 8000 0040  UNDEFINED
12668: IOC_STAT0    Status 0                   1 8000 0060  UNDEFINED
12669: IOC_STAT1    Status 1                   1 8000 0080  UNDEFINED
12670: IOC_TBIA     Translation buffer         1 8000 00A0  UNDEFINED
12671:              invalidate all             1 8000 00C0  The TLB is UNDEFINED and
12672: IOC_TB_ENA   Translation buffer enable               must be initialized by software.
12673: IOC_SFT_RST  PCI soft reset             1 8000 00E0  UNDEFINED
12674:                                                      The soft reset bit, and
12675: IOC_PAR_DIS Parity disable              1 8000 0100  consequently the PCI rst_l
12676: IOC_W_BASE0 Window base 0                            signal, will be asserted during
12677:                                         1 8000 0120  and after reset until modified
